gbtq-slang?p=883507#post883507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think a good question to ask, going back to the OP, is how do we define a slur in this case. I think it's the reason the thread got derailed, due to an argument over if a term had negative meaning or not. I'm not sure I know the exact answer, and if you answer it, it should help at narrowing down the field. This is just a thought, but it feels like the best way to hopefully bring it back without being derailed again.<br /> <br /> And I don't mean dictionary definition, as those aren't always of the greatest use when dealing with social issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. What might be a slur to me, may not be a slur to you, or someone else...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}